# ai-personal-tools monorepo (AI Personal Tools)

Bun workspaces (`apps/*`, `packages/*`). Runtime: **Bun 1.3.2**. All packages are **ESM** (`"type": "module"`). TypeScript strict mode everywhere. Validation: **Zod 4** (see root `README.md`).

## Workspace map

| Package | Import as | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `packages/core` | `@repo/core/all` | Domain contracts: `JobPostingSchema`, `JobPostingEntityT`, enums (`WorkModel`, `EmploymentType`, `Seniority`). Framework-agnostic. No env vars. **Purity:** runtime code under `packages/core/src` imports **`zod` only**; `@repo/tsconfig` is dev-only for `tsconfig.json` extends — not for runtime imports. |
| `packages/agent` | `@repo/agent/all` | Firecrawl scrape/crawl wrappers. `scraper().execWithJsonAsync(...)` for single page; `crawler().execJson(...)` for multi-page. Always pass `outputSchema` (Zod) + `prompt`. |
| `packages/db-ai` | `@repo/db-ai/all` | Prisma 6 + MongoDB. `jobPostingRepo().add(...)` persists `JobPostingEntityT`. Generated artifacts in `generated/` (git-ignored) — run `db-gen` after schema changes. |
| `packages/infra` | `@repo/infra/all` | Shared utilities: `zodHelper`, `pollCrawl`, `strToDate`, terminal helpers, file utils, branded results. No app-specific logic here. |
| `packages/ts` | `@repo/tsconfig/<preset>` | Shared TS presets (JSON): `tsConfigBunHono`, `tsConfigReactApp`, **`tsConfigReactLib`** (file on disk: `tsConfigReactLibrary.json`). Config-only, no runtime code. |
| `apps/ai-personal-tools-cli` | — | Interactive Ink + React terminal app. See `ai-personal-tools-cli` rule. |

## Dependency direction (enforce strictly)

```
apps/ai-personal-tools-cli
  -> @repo/agent  @repo/db-ai  @repo/core  @repo/infra
packages/agent, packages/db-ai
  -> @repo/core  @repo/infra (where applicable)  @repo/tsconfig (dev)
@repo/infra, @repo/core
  -> leaf packages: no imports from apps, agent, or db-ai
```

- **Nothing under `packages/*` may import from `apps/*`.** Apps consume packages; not the reverse.
- `@repo/core` and `@repo/infra` are leaf packages — they must not import from `agent`, `db-ai`, or any app.
- Apps must not import Prisma or Firecrawl directly; use `@repo/db-ai` and `@repo/agent` respectively.

## How packages communicate (summary)

| From | To | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| App `*.service.ts` | `@repo/agent` | `scraper().execWithJsonAsync` / `crawler().execJson` + Zod |
| App | `@repo/core` | `JobPostingSchema`, enums, `JobPostingEntityT` |
| App | `@repo/db-ai` | `jobPostingRepo()`, `tbZodSchema` when needed |
| App / `@repo/agent` | `@repo/infra` | helpers (`zodHelper`, `pollCrawl`, files, terminal) |
| `@repo/db-ai` | `@repo/core` | Persist shapes aligned with `JobPostingEntityT` |

## Import rules (ESLint-enforced)

- **Always use public entrypoints:** `import { … } from '@repo/<pkg>/all'`
- **Never** import from `@repo/*/src/**` or `packages/*/src/**`
- **Type-only imports:** `import type { … }` — keep separate from value imports

## Functional programming (enforced)

This codebase uses a **functional style throughout**. OOP patterns are not used.

**Never use:**
- `class` declarations (no classes anywhere in apps or packages)
- `this` keyword
- `new` for domain/service/repo objects (exception: third-party SDK constructors like `new Firecrawl(...)`)
- Inheritance or mixins

**Always use:**
- Plain functions and factory functions that return plain objects
- Zod schemas as the single source of truth for data shapes — no class-based models
- Immutable data flow: transform and return new values, do not mutate arguments
- `type` aliases over `interface` (ESLint-enforced)

**Factory function pattern** (the standard in this repo):

```ts
// ✅ correct — factory returns a plain object of functions
export function jobPostingRepo() {
  async function add(data: JobPostingEntityT) { … }
  return { add }
}

// ✅ correct — plain exported function
export async function jobPostingExtractCtrl({ url, … }: PropsT) { … }

// ❌ wrong — class with methods
export class JobPostingRepo {
  async add(data: JobPostingEntityT) { … }
}
```

**Module-level singletons** are fine for stateless shared values (e.g. `export const terminal = clackTerminalAdapter()`).

## Naming conventions (ESLint-aligned)

- **Variables and constants** (`let`, `const`, function parameters, and other bindings): **camelCase** (e.g. `userId`, `maxRetries`, `isReady`). Do not use `SCREAMING_SNAKE` for these names. **Exception:** React components stay **`PascalCase`** (see below).
- Types: `PascalCase` + `T` suffix (e.g. `JobPostingEntityT`)
- Type parameters: `T` prefix (e.g. `TItem`)
- Prefer `type` over `interface` unless declaration merging is needed
- React components: `PascalCase`

## Code style

- 2-space indent; single quotes; JSX attributes double quotes
- LF line endings; ~100 char line length
- No `any`; no empty catches; prefix unused vars with `_`
- **Imports spacing:** After the last `import` at the top of each file, insert **three empty lines** before the first following statement (local convention — same as “three blank lines between the import block and the first statement”).

## Package scripts reference

All commands run from the **package directory** unless noted.

### All packages (`@repo/core`, `@repo/agent`, `@repo/infra`, `@repo/db-ai`, `@repo/tsconfig`)

| Script | Command | When to run |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `lint` | `bunx eslint . --max-warnings 0` | After any code change |
| `check-types` | `bunx tsc --noEmit` | After any code change |
| `exports` | `barrelsby --delete --singleQuotes --noSemicolon --c barrels.config.json` | After adding/removing exported symbols |
| `exports-clean` | PowerShell: remove all `src/**/index.ts` then run barrelsby | Full barrel regeneration from scratch |

Run from repo root with filter:

```bash
bun run --filter @repo/<pkg> lint
bun run --filter @repo/<pkg> check-types
```

### `@repo/db-ai` only

| Script | Command | When to run |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `db-gen` | `bunx prisma generate` | After editing `schema.prisma` — regenerates Prisma client + Zod schemas in `generated/` |
| `db-push` | `bunx --bun prisma db push` | After `db-gen` — syncs schema to the database (dev only) |
| `db:migrate` | `bun src/migrations/run.ts` | Run ordered **custom TypeScript** migration scripts (not Prisma Migrate folders) |

### `apps/ai-personal-tools-cli`

| Script | Command | When to run |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `lint` | `bunx eslint . --max-warnings 0` | After any code change |
| `check-types` | `bunx tsc --noEmit` | After any code change |
| `dev` | `cd ../.. && bun run --hot apps/ai-personal-tools-cli/src/main.tsx` | Development with hot reload |
| `terminal` | `cd ../.. && bun run apps/ai-personal-tools-cli/src/main.tsx` | Single run |
| `exports` / `exports-clean` | barrelsby (same as packages) | After adding/removing exported symbols |

## MANDATORY: lint and type-check workflow

**After every code modification**, run lint and check-types for every package/app touched. This is not optional.

```
1. Make code changes
2. Run: bun run lint        (in the package/app directory)
3. Run: bun run check-types (in the package/app directory)
4. If errors → fix them → go to step 2
5. Repeat until both commands exit with 0 errors and 0 warnings
```

- **Zero warnings policy**: `--max-warnings 0` means any ESLint warning is a failure.
- **Fix, don't suppress**: do not add `// eslint-disable` or `@ts-ignore` to silence errors — fix the root cause.
- If multiple packages were touched, run lint + check-types in each one.
- For `@repo/db-ai` schema changes: run `db-gen` first, then lint + check-types.

## @repo/core — domain contracts

Key exports: `JobPostingSchema`, `JobPostingEntityT`, `WorkModel`, `EmploymentType`, `Seniority`.
Schema changes impact all consumers — update downstream types/tests when fields change.

## @repo/agent — scraping

```ts
// Single page + JSON extraction
scraper().execWithJsonAsync({ url, outputSchema, prompt, onStatusUpdate })

// Multi-page crawl
crawler().execJson({ url, outputSchema, prompt, onStatusUpdateFn })
```

`agent.ts` is currently stubbed/commented out — do not rely on it.

## @repo/db-ai — persistence

- Database: MongoDB. Prisma maps camelCase fields to snake_case via `@map(...)`.
- `generated/` is git-ignored; always run `db-gen` after editing `schema.prisma`.
- **Custom migrations:** TypeScript scripts in `src/migrations/scripts/`. Append a new script and register it **in order** in `src/migrations/run.ts` (the `migrations` array). Never reorder or remove scripts that may already be applied in shared environments. No `_migrations` ledger in this repo — keep scripts idempotent where possible.
- Generated Zod aggregates (e.g. `tbZodSchema`) are available from `@repo/db-ai/all`.

## @repo/infra — utilities

Key exports: `zodHelper.addDescriptionsToShape(...)`, `pollCrawl(...)` (caller supplies Firecrawl client), `strToDate(...)`, `clackTerminal` adapter, branded ok/err results, file/async utils.
Keep this package free of app-specific logic.

## Environment (monorepo root `.env`)

`loadEnvFromRoot()` in `shell/loadEnv.ts` walks up from `cwd` to find `.env`. It **does not overwrite** keys already present in `process.env`. Root `envConfig.ts` validates the full schema on startup.

| Variable | Required | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ENV` | Yes | `dev` \| `hml` \| `prod` |
| `FIRE_CRAWL_API_KEY` | Yes | Firecrawl auth |
| `AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY` | Yes | AI gateway |
| `OPEN_ROUTER_KEY` | Yes | OpenRouter LLM |
| `DATABASE_URL` | Yes | MongoDB connection |
| `HUGGING_FACE_TOKEN` | Yes | e.g. Whisper/diarization (`videoToText` / CLI tooling) |
| `WHISPER_MODEL_PATH` | Yes | Default model path for video-to-text UI (bounds in `envConfig.ts`) |

